          },
          "code": "QUERY_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1770878975269",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770878975270_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "For the user query: `{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}`\n\nUse this response content as the source of truth: `{{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_OPPORTUNITY_APP_ADVISOR.$output.output}}`\n\n\nStrict data rules:\n\nOnly use data, values, fields, opportunities, actions, and insights that are explicitly present in the provided response content.\nDo not infer, calculate, summarize, or add any value unless it is directly supported by the provided response content.\nDo not invent facts, labels, opportunity names, IDs, amounts, dates, actions, or insights.\nIf a useful field is not present in the provided response content, omit it.\nPreserve the meaning of the original response.\nClean up formatting only when needed for readability.\n\nRules:\n- **Always** hightlight the main answer to the user query in Bold.\n- Do not include prefixes such as `Answer=`, `content=`, `Response=`, or similar labels.\n- Preserve the meaning of the original response.\n- Clean up formatting only when needed for readability.\n- Do not invent facts, values, opportunities, actions, or insights.\n- Do not wrap the response in code fences.\n- Do not include unrelated explanation.\n- Return the response with 1 ~ 3 widgets for easy display of the response. \n-  The supporting data / Additional insights should be added as markdown without the widget as a drop down\n- ** Do not ** repeat the same data n the widget and in additional insights. If it is include in the widget, remove the data from the additional insights\n\nWidget selection rules:\n- Choose the widget or widgets that best display the response for the user query.\n- If the response contains an `action` attribute, use it to enable an action on the widget.\n- When using an action, use the related opportunity name as the action text and Title of the widget. Choose available additional attributes or description as short desctiption.\n- If the response contains multiple opportunities, use a `Message List` or `Multi Record` widget.\n- If the user query asks for comparison, change, trend, increase, decrease, delta, or difference, use a `Change Widget`.\n- Use \"Card\" or \"Multi Card\" widget if the response needed 1 ~ 3 opportunities with few attributes.\n- If a visualization would make the answer easier to understand, add a `Chart` widget.\n- A `Chart` widget must always be additional. Do not use a chart as the only widget.\n- Always display the actual data in a non-chart widget when a chart is used."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Payload for Communication",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let commPtoFill =  $context.$app.$OraCommParamsToFill;\nlet commNonTemplate = $context.$app.$OraCommNonTemplateParamList;\nlet message = $context.$system.$inputMessage;\n\n\nlet retObj = {}\nretObj.draftFlag = true;\nretObj.subject = commNonTemplate.find(com=>com.id ==\"subject\").value??\"No Subject\";\nretObj.body = message;\nretObj.trackConversationFlag = true;\nretObj.providerCode = \"EXCHANGE\";\nretObj.toAddress = commNonTemplate.find(com=>com.id ==\"email\").value??\"email@email.com\";\nretObj.conversationReferences=`ORA_MOO_OPTY.${commNonTemplate.find(com=>com.id ==\"optyid\")?.value??\"\"}`;\nretObj.messageTemplateObjTypeCd =\"ORA_MOO_OPTY\";\nretObj.msgTemplateObjectId = commNonTemplate.find(com=>com.id ==\"optyid\")?.value??\"\";\n\nreturn retObj;  "
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1774374663144"
          },
