          "code": "ACTION_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1776463026330",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776463026330_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Based on {{$context.$nodes.REFINE_RESPONSE_FROM_ASSISTANT.$output.result}}, which has the structure: {\n\"type\": <Type>, \"message\": { \"primaryText\": <primaryText>, \"secondaryText\": <secondaryText>, \"postback\": <postback> } }\n\nIf the type is \"text\", generate a professional single-line sentence stating that no data insights were found to process the action and no action and communication will be created.\n\nIf the type is \"chip\":\n- Format primaryText as a markdown Header Level 3 (###).\n- Format secondaryText as a markdown Header Level 4 (####).\n- Format postback as markdown content.\n\nAlso, Produce a PowerPoint communication with the following:\n  - Format primaryText as a markdown Header Level 3 (###).\n  - Format secondaryText as a markdown Header Level 4 (####).\n  - Format postback as markdown content.\n- Ensure the PowerPoint slides are well-organized and content is easily readable.\n- If the content is too long for one slide, split it into multiple slides to maintain clarity and readability.\n\nAdditionally, produce one email communication with \ntitle: Email: {{$context.$nodes.BUILD_PAYLOAD_FOR_ASSISTANT.$output.result.title}},\nactionText: ‘Send Email’\ndescription: one sentence summarizing the email’s intent\ntargetAgent: 'ORA_OPPORTUNITY_HEALTH_AND_PRIORITIZATION',\nemailSubject: {{$context.$nodes.BUILD_PAYLOAD_FOR_ASSISTANT.$output.result.title}}\nand the data format with html: {{$context.$nodes.REFINE_RESPONSE_FROM_ASSISTANT.$output.result}}\nand Close:\n   Best regards,<br/>\nFull name from {{$context.$app.$OraUserContext}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1776463026330_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an assistant that generates communication content based on user input.\nWhen both PowerPoint communication and email communication are requested, create each\nseparately and clearly separate their outputs. Do not mix content from PowerPoint and email\ncommunications in the same output. Ensure that each communication type is distinctly\nlabeled or formatted so the user can easily identify and use them independently.\n\nFollow these rules strictly to avoid any confusion between the two communication types.\n\nUse concise and clear language for each output section.\n\nMaintain all existing prompt template rules and expression formats as provided."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Display Attributes",
            "policyCode": "ORA_OPPORTUNITY_PRIORITIZATION_POLICY",
